#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""run.py <case_id> | run.py --validate-only [isvcs_dir]

Watcher-driven test runner for the OMENative rollout playground.
--validate-only checks the whole case tree (id uniqueness + line-1 header
schema) with zero cluster interaction and exits nonzero on any problem.

Architecture:
  1. Apply the ISVC; read its (post-defaulting) spec: per-Component update
     strategy + the spec.rollout.groups (OEP-0017 v2; the harness derives a
     synthetic policy / members / order / soak from the group shapes).
  2. Start `kubectl get pod -w -o json --output-watch-events`; read events line-
     by-line, maintaining a per-pod state map (comp, alive, ready, hash, uid,
     newanno). Compute per-Component (alive, ready, updated) counts.
  3. State machine:
       INIT      → wait until every configured Component has N complete
                   Instances Ready+serving and its IR reports a settled revision.
       (trigger) → snapshot OLD revision hashes + pod UIDs, then bump the
                   `perm.test/rev` annotation on EVERY group member (engine-only
                   when there is no coordination group), or on the `bump=`
                   members alone. → ROTATING
       ROTATING  → wait until every Component is back at N alive AND N ready, AND
                   every BUMPED Component has all N pods on the new revision,
                   sustained STABILITY_S.
       CONVERGED → stop watcher, emit verdict.
  4. Throughout: track peak alive per Component, and per-Component first-change /
     fully-rotated timestamps (for Sequential ordering + soak verification).
  5. Throughout (every mode, whole case duration): continuous invariants —
     (A) status-truth: no IR Instance claims Failed while all its pods serve, or
     Ready with no pods; (B) endpoints-membership: every serving pod is a Ready
     endpoint of its per-revision routed Service and no endpoint references a
     deleted pod; (C) pair-alive (armed only by mode=pairing for a non-empty→
     non-empty protocol transition): whenever both engine and decoder serve, a
     pairable pair exists; (F) label-truth: every pod runs the template its
     revision-hash label names; (G) ready-serving: an Instance the IR reports
     Ready has a pod in rotation; (H) superseded-revision: once a rollout
     reports done, no Instance runs another revision. Sustained violations
     FAIL the verdict (INV_*).
  6. Optional fault injection (header fault=<kind>:<param>): quota:<n> (derived
     ResourceQuota admitting exactly +n case-shaped pods), podkill:<phase>,
     ctrlrestart:<phase> (gated on OME_TEST_ALLOW_CTRL_RESTART=1), cordon:source,
     repeat=<n> (a podkill, an eviction, the kill of mode=kill or a manager
     restart applied again each time what it took has come back, n times,
     then lifted: the persistent form, judged across the window and after),
     crashloop:old (one old-revision pod of victimcomp= made to crash on every
     start, form=start, or after Ready, form=load) and imagepull:old (the same
     pod pointed at an image that cannot be pulled), both from the moment the
     bump lands; the verdict requires that Instance to end on the new revision
     with no repair recorded for it (a victim nobody bumped must be rebuilt by
     a recorded repair instead). during=idle fires a persistent fault on the
     settled service with no bump: a break is read as expect=repaired|held,
     configkey:missing (the runner's ConfigMap key removed and the runner
     restarted, put back at lift=after-settle|after-failed) as
     expect=heals|parked, node:notready (the victim's KIND node kubelet
     stopped, started again at lift=after-settle|after-failed|after-recover)
     as expect=relocated|repaired|parked, or SKIP where this host's docker
     does not own the nodes; needs=forcedelete|no-forcedelete names the
     force-delete policy the outcome is read against, SKIP where the
     readiness:old with form=persist|recover sets the
     fixture's readiness switch in one serving pod (it runs, leaves rotation,
     is never rebuilt; recover lifts the switch and the same pod returns);
     readiness:new bumps a revision whose pods never pass readiness (the roll
     holds at the ready timeout, then a fix push lands). podkill takes
     kill=leader|worker and victim=stable|canary on gangs and fires at
     draining too; floor_slack=<k> lowers the floor by the Instances a fault
     takes. cordon:all with lift=after-hold|never squeezes a roll out of room
     (the wait must name the capacity, nothing is torn down to make room,
     the roll completes once the squeeze lifts). Apparatus errors record the
     distinct INFRA-FAIL verdict — harness infrastructure broke, not the
     product. during=idle in mode=scaledown and mode=recreate breaks one
     Instance of the running revision first (crashloop:old, imagepull:old,
     or readiness:old form=persist: the fixture's readiness switch set in
     the live pod; inst= names the Instance) and lands the scale or the
     delete once the status has reported it; the verdict reads the
     operator's order of removal, the untouched survivors, the healthy
     capacity, the fate of the broken Instance on a scale-up
     (expect=repaired|left) and the rows settling with no operation open.
  7. Optional mid-roll edit (edit=strategy:<type> | edit=restartPolicy:<policy>
     at during=settling|rotating): every bumped member's lifecycle is patched
     at the hook, and the verdict adds that the edit was applied and landed.
  8. Optional rollback (rollback=1 at during=settling|rotating|draining|last|
     held): the revision the run started from is re-applied on every bumped
     member at the hook (held: break=stuck gives the new revision a readiness
     probe it never passes, so the roll parks at its budget first), and the
     verdict is the operator's end state: every Instance back on the starting
     revision and serving, no pod of the new revision left, the controller's
     rows settled with no open operation, and on a grouped service the run
     that targeted the new revision closed as superseded.
  9. Operations on a stuck Component (stuck=held|failed with img=, in
     mode=scaledown|recreate): the bumped members are pushed onto a revision
     that cannot be pulled, the handler waits for the first failed attempt or
     for the spent retry ladder, and only then scales or deletes; the verdict
     reads the engine's victim order, the untouched survivors, the healthy
     capacity, and the push the status must keep reporting.
 10. A runtime edit and a repair overlapping (mode=runtimerev with a break
     fault): the crash lands as the edit does and the roll owns it, or with
     during=repair the edit lands while the repair's replacement pod comes up;
     either way every Instance ends on the edited revision, the repaired one
     is rebuilt at most once after the edit, and no row is left mid-operation.

Why bump ALL group members (the 2026-06-01 fix):
  OMENative coordination is a status-only layer + *restrictive* gates. It never
  *initiates* a roll on a Component whose template did not change; each Component
  rolls off its OWN revision hash. The contract (OEP-0007.1) is that the operator
  bumps every member's template and coordination then sequences/paces/flips the
  resulting per-member rolls. Bumping only the engine therefore rolls only the
  engine — by design. To exercise coordination at all, the trigger must perturb
  every member. (The earlier "decoder never surged ⇒ coordination broken" verdict
  was a harness false positive, not a controller bug.)

Update detection per strategy:
  * surge/recreate (SurgeThenDrain / RecreatePod): a pod is "updated" once it
    carries a revision-hash NOT present pre-trigger (a brand-new pod).
  * in-place (InPlaceIfPossible / InPlaceOnly): an annotation diff is patched
    onto the LIVE pod — same UID, same revision-hash label — so hash-watching is
    blind to it. Instead a pod is "updated" once it carries the new
    `perm.test/rev=v2` annotation, and we separately assert its UID never rotated.
"""
import datetime
import json
import math
import os
import queue
import re
import select
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import threading
import time
import urllib.parse
import uuid
from collections import defaultdict
from pathlib import Path

import irstatus
import runtime_fixtures

# Env-driven so the harness isn't pinned to one cluster (see batch.py).
KUBECONFIG = os.environ.get("OME_TEST_KUBECONFIG") or os.environ.get("KUBECONFIG") or os.path.expanduser("~/.kube/config")
# Shared per-run stamp: all of a run's results live under results/<RUN_TS>/.
# batch.py exports OME_RUN_TS so its parallel subprocesses share one run folder;
# a standalone run.py generates its own.
RUN_TS = os.environ.get("OME_RUN_TS") or time.strftime("%Y%m%d-%H%M%S")
NS = os.environ.get("OME_TEST_NS", "sandbox")
HERE = Path(__file__).parent.resolve()
REV_LABEL = "ome.io/revision-hash"   # OMENative per-revision pod label (query.LabelRevisionHash)
PAIRING_LABEL = "ome.io/pairing-protocol"  # P/D pairing cohort label (query.LabelPairingProtocol):
                                           # on pods (render + in-place restamp) and per-revision
                                           # routing Services (metadata only — never the selector)
TRIGGER_ANNO = "perm.test/rev"       # annotation we bump to trigger a rollout
TRIGGER_VAL = "v2"
PROMOTE_ANNO = "ome.io/rollout-promote"    # canary manual-promote verb (value = canary revision hash)
ROLLBACK_ANNO = "ome.io/rollout-rollback"  # canary rollback verb (drain to stable + sticky hold)
STABILITY_S = 5     # require target sustained this many seconds before CONVERGED
SEQ_TOL_S = 6       # ordering/soak slack (1Hz sampling + readiness jitter)
GANG_TOL_S = 5.0    # multi-node gang grace: a leader+worker Instance may look mixed-revision
                    # only this briefly during a fast gang flip; sustained longer = piecemeal roll
MINREADY_GRACE_S = 3.0  # skip the first few s after trigger (INIT→ROTATING boundary) before
                        # tracking min ready Instances vs the N - maxUnavailable capacity floor
RATIO_EPS = 0.10    # RatioBalanced band grace for 1Hz sampling jitter + surge transients
RATIO_SUSTAIN_S = 5.0  # assert the worst ratio deviation that PERSISTED this long, not the
                       # instantaneous spike. The gate is eventually-consistent (engine/decoder
                       # on separate dispatchers, peer status lags a reconcile), so when both move
                       # opposite directions a bounded ~1-2s cross-dispatcher overshoot is by-design
                       # and self-corrects. Only an off-band deviation held >= this window is real.
FLOOR_SUSTAIN_S = 5.0  # capacity-floor debounce (mirrors RATIO_SUSTAIN_S): the hard floor check
                       # fails only on a below-floor dip that PERSISTED this long — a single-sample
                       # readiness flap at 1Hz must not red a case. floor_hard=1 skips the debounce.
# Migration source-drain settle budget: mult-scaled + per-migrated-instance,
# defined below alongside the other TIMEOUT_MULT budgets (needs TIMEOUT_MULT).
TEARDOWN_BASE_S, TEARDOWN_PER_POD_S = 120, 5   # post-delete teardown-convergence budget
TEARDOWN_POLL_S = 5.0

# ── Continuous invariants (status-truth + endpoints-membership + …) ─────────
# Polled for the WHOLE duration of every case, in every mode. API-load bound
# (shared cluster): the poller reads at most 4 label-selected namespaced GETs
# per tick per running case — one InferenceReplica list (invariants A, G, H),
# one Service list + one EndpointSlice list (B, G), one ISVC status (H) — plus
# a ControllerRevision list only while a live pod carries a revision hash the
# label-truth ledger (F) has not read yet. Pod state is reused from the
# watcher (no extra pod reads). At INV_TICK_S=5 that is 0.8 req/s per case,
# ~6.5 req/s at batch conc-8 — the same order as the existing status polls
# (canary 0.5/s, migrate ledger 0.2/s).
INV_TICK_S = 5.0
INV_SUSTAIN_D = 6    # gang-scheduling ticks (30 s): a gang half-bound this long is not still arriving
SCHED_NAME = os.environ.get("OME_EVAL_SCHEDULER", "").strip()   # non-empty: invariant D asserts gang scheduling
# Sustain counts, in CONSECUTIVE tick observations — the transient carve-out:
#   A (status-truth): 2 observations = the condition spanned >= 1 full tick
#     interval (>= 5s; fires 5-10s after onset depending on tick phase), so a
#     just-transitioned phase — read while the controller is mid-flip — can
#     never fire off a single stale sample.
#   B missing-endpoint: 3 observations = the gap spanned >= 2 tick intervals
#     (>= (3-1)*5 = 10s; fires 10-15s after onset). Endpoint controllers lag
#     pod readiness legitimately (slice mirror + kube-proxy churn, normally
#     1-2s); any propagation lag < 10s cannot span 3 consecutive ticks.
#   B stale-endpoint (deleted pod UID still referenced): 2 observations
#     (5-10s), same arithmetic as A — slice purge is near-immediate.
INV_SUSTAIN_A = 2
INV_SUSTAIN_B_MISSING = 3
INV_SUSTAIN_B_STALE = 2
# C pair-alive: 2 observations (>= 1 full tick interval), same arithmetic as A.
# A REAL pair break lasts at least one pod-startup cycle (the new cohort must
# come Ready before a pair can re-form), so it always spans 2+ ticks; a
# single-sample race between a label restamp and a serving flip cannot.
INV_SUSTAIN_C = 2
# IR Instance phases exempt from ALL status-truth checks: transitional by
# definition. A Migrating source keeps serving while its replacement surges;
# Updating/Restarting/Creating/Deleting all legitimately hold pods in states
# that would read as a lie if sampled mid-transition.
INV_TRANSIENT_PHASES = {"Pending", "Creating", "Updating", "Restarting", "Migrating", "Deleting"}
SERVING_COND = "ome.io/serving"   # controller-managed pod readiness gate (query.ServingConditionType)
# The invariant classes a header may waive (inv_off) or park (inv_xfail). E,
# the cohort-ratio observer, is informational and never fails, so it is not
# a class here. J (no auto-recovery record) and K (no node exclusion) are
# opt-in: a header selects them with inv_on=J,K.
INV_OPT_IN = {"J", "K"}
INV_CLASSES = {"A", "B", "C", "D", "F", "G", "H"} | INV_OPT_IN
INV_NAMES = {"A": "status-truth", "B": "endpoints-membership", "C": "pair-alive", "D": "gang-scheduling",
             "F": "label-truth", "G": "ready-serving", "H": "superseded-revision",
             "J": "no-auto-recovery", "K": "no-node-exclusion"}
# The audit ledger ConfigMap the engine keeps per service, and the record it
# writes when it gives up on an Instance's node and steers the rebuild
# elsewhere. Invariant J reads it.
AUDIT_LEDGER_SUFFIX = "-ome-migration-audit"
AUDIT_LEDGER_KEY = "history.json"
AUTO_RECOVER_REASON = "AutoRecover"
HOSTNAME_LABEL = "kubernetes.io/hostname"

# Dynamic timeouts: real kubelet + a 15s artificial startup sleep per pod, and
# surge=1 rolls serialize. Static 240s was too tight for N=8 and for two-member
# Sequential rolls (decoder fully, soak, then engine).
# OME_TEST_TIMEOUT_MULT scales every init/rotate budget for a loaded cluster
# where scheduling + CPU-throttled startup drag past the default budgets (a
# busy shared cluster can take 3-4x longer to schedule N=8 than an idle one).
# Default 1.0; set e.g. 2.5 when a smoke run shows INIT_TIMEOUT dominated by
# slow scheduling rather than product non-convergence.
try:
    TIMEOUT_MULT = max(1.0, float(os.environ.get("OME_TEST_TIMEOUT_MULT", "1.0")))
except ValueError:
    TIMEOUT_MULT = 1.0
INIT_BASE_S, INIT_PER_POD_S = int(120 * TIMEOUT_MULT), int(25 * TIMEOUT_MULT)
# Sequential 2-member rolls serialize (decoder fully, then engine) and under
# conc-8 cluster load creep to ~400s for 8 bumped pods; 40s/pod (=410s budget)
# left no headroom for the trailing STABILITY_S window (p34 converged at 406s
# but timed out at 410s before "stable"). 60s/pod gives comfortable margin.
ROTATE_BASE_S, ROTATE_PER_POD_S = int(180 * TIMEOUT_MULT), int(100 * TIMEOUT_MULT)
MAX_BUDGET_S = int(1800 * TIMEOUT_MULT)
# kill-mode pause handling: settle after annotating (annotation → IR
# projection → workload input), and the no-recovery hold window a paused
# case must survive before the lift step.
PAUSE_PROJECT_S = int(15 * TIMEOUT_MULT)
KILL_PAUSE_HOLD_S = int(60 * TIMEOUT_MULT)
# Settle window shared by the invariants whose condition the controller may
# pass through briefly on its way to the truth — F (an in-place update patches
# images, labels and annotations in separate writes), G (the serving flip and
# endpoint propagation after a pod turns Ready), H (the run close and the next
# render). A condition fires only once observed on consecutive ticks spanning
# at least INV_SETTLE_S, which scales with the cluster budget like every wait.
INV_SETTLE_S = 15.0 * TIMEOUT_MULT
INV_SUSTAIN_SETTLE = 1 + math.ceil(INV_SETTLE_S / INV_TICK_S)
# Post-Completed source-drain grace. A source can't drain until its surge
# replacement is Ready (~one pod-init cycle), and multi-instance migrations
# SERIALIZE on a surge budget of 1 (reusing freed indices), so the drain is
# O(migrated-instances), not flat. Budget = base + per-instance, both
# mult-scaled — mirrors the INIT/ROTATE budget shape. A flat 90s spuriously
# reds every 2+-instance migration on a loaded cluster even though the ledger
# records each migration Completed correctly.
MIGRATE_SETTLE_BASE_S, MIGRATE_SETTLE_PER_INST_S = int(90 * TIMEOUT_MULT), int(90 * TIMEOUT_MULT)


def migrate_settle_budget(n_insts):
    """Source-drain settle ceiling for a migration of n_insts instances."""
    return min(MAX_BUDGET_S, MIGRATE_SETTLE_BASE_S + MIGRATE_SETTLE_PER_INST_S * max(1, n_insts))

IN_PLACE_TYPES = {"InPlaceIfPossible", "InPlaceOnly"}
# The fixture runtimes' main container. A leader runner override must name
# it (the CRD requires a name there), and readiness is read off it.
MAIN_CONTAINER = "ome-container"
# Strategies whose replacement is up before the source leaves serving: a surge
# drains only after its replacement is Ready, an in-place op returns the same
# pod. Everything else (RecreatePod) is drain-first: nothing comes up until
# something goes down, which is the only shape where an unpaired window at
# 1x1 is unavoidable.
REPLACEMENT_FIRST_TYPES = {"SurgeThenDrain"} | IN_PLACE_TYPES


def _pairing_drain_first(info):
    """True when either pairing Component updates drain-first."""
    strat = info.get("strat") or {}
    return any((strat.get(c) or "SurgeThenDrain") not in REPLACEMENT_FIRST_TYPES for c in ("engine", "decoder"))
COMPS = ("engine", "decoder", "router")

TSV_HEADER = ("id\tdesc\tNe\tNd\tNr\tceil_e\tceil_d\tceil_r\tpeak_e\tpeak_d\tpeak_r\t"
              "final_e\tfinal_d\tfinal_r\tconv_secs\tpolicy\tverdict\tnote\tnew_e\tnew_d\tnew_r\n")


def kubectl(*args, env=None, **kw):
    env_full = {**os.environ, "KUBECONFIG": KUBECONFIG}
    if env:
        env_full.update(env)
    return subprocess.run(["kubectl", *args], capture_output=True, text=True, env=env_full, **kw)


def apply_runtime_fixtures():
    """Apply the runtime fixtures into NS, idempotently.

    They are templates rather than literal YAML: the PVC, its seed Job and the
    ClusterBaseModel's storageUri all have to name NS, because a pod cannot
    mount a PVC from another namespace and the ISVC validator rejects a model
    that points at one.
    """
    return kubectl("apply", "--validate=false", "-n", NS, "-f", "-", check=False,
                   input=runtime_fixtures.render(kind=runtime_fixtures.kind_from_env()))


def _fixture_values():
    return runtime_fixtures.resolve(kind=runtime_fixtures.kind_from_env())


def render_case(yaml_file):
    """The case manifest with its fixture tokens (image registry, node arch)
    resolved for the target cluster, exactly as the shared runtime fixtures are."""
    return runtime_fixtures.render_text(Path(yaml_file).read_text(), _fixture_values())


# The admission webhook reads runtimes through a cache. A case that ships its
# own ServingRuntime creates it in the same apply as its InferenceService, so
# the validator can see the ISVC before the runtime and deny it as unsupported.
# That denial, and only that one, is re-applied for a short window.
RUNTIME_LAG_DENIAL = "does not support model"
RUNTIME_LAG_WINDOW_S = 30


def apply_case(yaml_file):
    body = render_case(yaml_file)
    ships_runtime = re.search(r"^kind:\s*(Cluster)?ServingRuntime\s*$", body, re.M) is not None
    deadline = time.monotonic() + RUNTIME_LAG_WINDOW_S
    while True:
        r = kubectl("apply", "--validate=false", "-n", NS, "-f", "-", input=body)
        if (r.returncode == 0 or not ships_runtime
                or RUNTIME_LAG_DENIAL not in (r.stderr or "")
                or time.monotonic() >= deadline):
            return r
        time.sleep(2)


def delete_case(yaml_file):
    if yaml_file is None:   # nothing was ever applied
        return None
    return kubectl("delete", "-n", NS, "-f", "-", "--wait=false", input=render_case(yaml_file))


def parse_header(path):
    """First line of YAML has comment header with Ne=N Nd=N Nr=N ceil_e=N ceil_d=N ceil_r=N."""
    with open(path) as f:
        first = f.readline().lstrip("#").strip()
    first = runtime_fixtures.substitute(first, _fixture_values())
    fields = {}
    for tok in first.split():
        if "=" in tok and not tok.startswith("("):
            k, _, v = tok.partition("=")
            try:
                fields[k] = int(v)
            except ValueError:
                fields[k] = v
    return first, fields


def parse_duration(v):
    """metav1.Duration-ish: '30s' '1m' '500ms' or a bare number → seconds (int)."""
    if v is None:
        return 0
    if isinstance(v, (int, float)):
        return int(v)
    s = str(v).strip()
    try:
        if s.endswith("ms"):
            return int(float(s[:-2]) / 1000)
        if s.endswith("s"):
            return int(float(s[:-1]))
        if s.endswith("m"):
            return int(float(s[:-1]) * 60)
        if s.endswith("h"):
            return int(float(s[:-1]) * 3600)
        return int(float(s))
    except ValueError:
        return 0


def resolve_max_unavailable(mu, n):
    """maxUnavailable → absolute Instance count against n, resolved as the
    engine resolves a per-Component budget (resolve_budget, shared with
    maxSurge): ints pass through, clamped at 0; percent strings are
    ceil(n * percent / 100), clamped to n, so '25%' of 8 = 2, '100%' of 8 = 8,
    and at the small sizes '50%' of 1 and '25%' of 2 are both 1 (a positive
    percent never rounds to zero). Anything unparsable = 0."""
    return resolve_budget(mu, n)


def resolve_budget(value, n):
    """A rolling-update budget (maxSurge or maxUnavailable) as an absolute
    Instance count against n: the per-Component rounding rule the engine
    applies to both, a percent rounded up and clamped to n."""
    if isinstance(value, int):
        return max(0, value)
    s = str(value).strip()
    if s.endswith("%"):
        try:
            return max(0, min(n, -(-n * int(float(s[:-1])) // 100)))
        except ValueError:
            return 0
    try:
        return max(0, int(s))
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return 0


def canary_unit(comp):
    """The canary unit a Component belongs to, named by the unit's entrypoint.

    The router is its own unit; engine and decoder are one unit, because a P/D
    pair speaks a pairing protocol to each other. A unit is what one canary run
    owns — its step counter, revision pair and traffic entry live on the
    entrypoint. Mirrors rollout.CanaryUnit.
    """
    return "engine" if comp == "decoder" else comp


def canary_unit_entrypoint(components):
    """The Component a canary group's step machine is driven through: the
    entrypoint of the unit the group covers. Mirrors canary.primaryComponent."""
    for c in ("router", "engine", "decoder"):
        if c in components:
            return c
    return ""


def get_spec_info(case_id):
    """Read spec.rollout.groups + per-Component update strategy from the live ISVC.

    Returns dict: {policy, members, order, soak, pacing, ratio_tol, strat:{comp:type},
    canary, ...}. The v2 group shapes are projected back onto the legacy synthetic
    'policy'/'pacing' fields the verdict logic keys on (see the mapping below).
    """
    info = {"policy": None, "members": [], "order": [], "soak": 0, "strat": {},
            "pacing": None, "ratio_tol": None, "workers": {}, "max_unavail": {}, "partition": {},
            "canary": None, "canary_groups": [], "pairing": ""}
    r = kubectl("-n", NS, "get", "isvc", case_id, "-o", "json")
    if r.returncode != 0:
        return info
    try:
        spec = json.loads(r.stdout).get("spec", {})
    except Exception:
        return spec_default(info)
    for c in COMPS:
        cs = spec.get(c)
        if isinstance(cs, dict):
            t = cs.get("lifecycle", {}).get("updateStrategy", {}).get("type", "SurgeThenDrain")
            info["strat"][c] = t or "SurgeThenDrain"
            # Multi-node: a Component with worker.size>0 runs each Instance as
            # 1 leader + worker.size worker pods (otherwise a single 'default'
            # pod). Drives pods-per-Instance for the Instance-level counters.
            w = cs.get("worker")
            if isinstance(w, dict) and w.get("size"):
                info["workers"][c] = int(w["size"])
            # Per-Component maxUnavailable → the capacity floor (Check 10).
            # Stored RAW (int or percent string); every consumer resolves it
            # against N via resolve_max_unavailable so "100%"/"25%" cases get
            # their real floor instead of silently reading as 0.
            ru = cs.get("lifecycle", {}).get("updateStrategy", {}).get("rollingUpdate", {})
            info["max_unavail"][c] = ru.get("maxUnavailable", 0)
            pt = ru.get("partition", 0)
            info["partition"][c] = pt if isinstance(pt, int) else 0
    # OEP-0017 (v2): coordination + canary unified under spec.rollout.groups[].
    # The harness verdict logic still keys on a synthetic 'policy' (+ pacing,
    # ratio_tol, members, order, soak) and a separate 'canary' block, so derive
    # those legacy fields from the v2 group shapes:
    #   - a single .blueGreen group              -> policy "BlueGreen"
    #   - .rollingUpdate group                   -> policy "RollingUpdate"
    #       + .maintainRatio                     -> pacing "RatioBalanced" (ratio_tol = tolerance)
    #   - .canary group                          -> info["canary"] (not a coordination policy)
    #   - MULTIPLE single-Component blueGreen     -> policy "Sequential" (members/order = the chain)
    #     groups, one per component, in list order  (the v2 spelling for Sequential)
    # P/D pairing protocol (opaque cohort token; rides every engine/decoder
    # revision). "" = unset = pairs with anything.
    info["pairing"] = str(spec.get("rollout", {}).get("pairingProtocol") or "")
    groups = spec.get("rollout", {}).get("groups", []) or []
    # Canary groups first (canary lives on a group; it's not a coordination
    # policy). One group per canary UNIT — an ISVC may carry a router run and an
    # engine run at once — so every canary group is recorded, keyed by its unit.
    # info["canary"]/["members"] keep naming the first for the legacy readers;
    # the canary handler selects its group out of canary_groups.
    for g in groups:
        if not (isinstance(g, dict) and isinstance(g.get("canary"), dict)):
            continue
        can, comps = g["canary"], (g.get("components", []) or [])
        cg = {
            "unit": canary_unit_entrypoint(comps),
            "members": comps,
            "order": g.get("order", []) or [],
            "policy": (str(can.get("promotion") or "").lower() or None),
            "steps": can.get("steps", []) or [],
            "readyTimeout": can.get("readyTimeout"),
        }
        info["canary_groups"].append(cg)
        if info["canary"] is None:
            info["canary"] = {"policy": cg["policy"], "steps": cg["steps"]}
            info["members"] = cg["members"]
            info["order"] = cg["order"]
    # Coordination groups (the non-canary ones).
    coord_groups = [g for g in groups if isinstance(g, dict) and not isinstance(g.get("canary"), dict)]
    bg_groups = [g for g in coord_groups if isinstance(g.get("blueGreen"), dict)]
    single_bg = [g for g in bg_groups if len(g.get("components", []) or []) == 1]
    if coord_groups and len(coord_groups) == len(single_bg) and len(single_bg) > 1:
        # Multiple single-Component blueGreen groups in order == Sequential.
        chain = [(g.get("components") or [None])[0] for g in single_bg]
        info["policy"] = "Sequential"
        info["members"] = [c for c in chain if c]
        info["order"] = list(info["members"])
        # Soak is carried on each step group; surface the first non-zero (the
        # harness uses a single soak value for its handoff-gap check).
        for g in single_bg:
            s = parse_duration(g.get("soak"))
            if s:
                info["soak"] = s
                break
    elif coord_groups:
        g = coord_groups[0]
        info["members"] = g.get("components", []) or []
        info["order"] = g.get("order", []) or []
        info["soak"] = parse_duration(g.get("soak"))
        if isinstance(g.get("blueGreen"), dict):
            info["policy"] = "BlueGreen"
        elif isinstance(g.get("rollingUpdate"), dict) or "rollingUpdate" in g:
            info["policy"] = "RollingUpdate"
            mr = g.get("maintainRatio")
            if isinstance(mr, dict):
                info["pacing"] = "RatioBalanced"
                info["ratio_tol"] = mr.get("tolerance")
    return info


def spec_default(info):
    return info


def update_modes(info, configured, edit=None):
    """Per-Component update mode the watcher counts by: "inplace" when the
    strategy patches the live pod (the new revision shows as the bumped
    annotation on the same pod), else "surge" (a new pod at a new revision
    hash). A rollout with a template edit (TEMPLATE_EDITS) changes the pod
    template beyond container images, so an in-place strategy resolves to a
    recreate and its pods are counted by hash like any drain-first roll; an
    image edit is the diff an in-place strategy patches, so it counts in
    place."""
    return {c: ("inplace" if info["strat"].get(c) in IN_PLACE_TYPES and edit not in TEMPLATE_EDITS else "surge")
            for c in configured}


def aggregate(state, old_hashes, modes, pods_per_inst, measures=None):
    """state: pod_name → {comp, inst, runner, alive, ready, hash, uid, newanno} | None.

    Groups pods into INSTANCES by (comp, instance-index) and returns
    {comp: (alive_inst, ready_inst, updated_inst)} counted in Instances, not raw
    pods. An Instance is one 'default' pod (single-pod) or 1 'leader' +
    worker.size 'worker' pods (multi-node); pods_per_inst[comp] is that expected
    per-Instance pod count. An Instance is:
      * alive   → it has >=1 pod (a surge adds a whole new Instance index);
      * ready   → it has its full pod set AND every pod is Ready;
      * updated → every pod moved to the new generation, per update mode:
          - surge   → pod's revision-hash is NOT in old_hashes (a new pod)
          - inplace → pod carries the new perm.test/rev annotation (same pod)
    Pre-trigger (old_hashes is None) updated is always 0. Backward-compatible:
    single-pod cases have one pod per Instance, so counts equal the old per-pod
    counts.

    measures (opt-in dict, mutated in place): per-Component distinct-alive-index
    diagnostics that the raw (alive,ready,updated) tuple cannot express. For each
    Component c it records {c: (distinct_alive_idx, new_pods, distinct_new_idx)}:
      * distinct_alive_idx → # of instance indices with >=1 alive pod. A gang
        surge that COLLAPSES many gangs onto ONE index reads as 1 distinct index
        even though the alive-pod count is large — the fleet-wipe signature the
        Instance-count tuple hides.
      * new_pods           → raw count of alive new-revision pods (post-trigger).
      * distinct_new_idx   → # of distinct indices carrying >=1 new-revision pod.
        For a healthy gang roll new_pods == distinct_new_idx * pods_per_inst; a
        shortfall means two gangs share an index (collision).
    """
    insts = defaultdict(lambda: defaultdict(list))  # comp -> instance-index -> [pod records]
    for p in state.values():
        if p is None or not p["alive"]:
            continue
        insts[p["comp"]][p.get("inst", "0")].append(p)
    agg = defaultdict(lambda: [0, 0, 0])
    for c, by_inst in insts.items():
        ppi = max(1, pods_per_inst.get(c, 1))
        distinct_alive_idx = new_pods = distinct_new_idx = 0
        for pods in by_inst.values():
            # alive: gangs count 1 per Instance (a surge is a whole new instance
            # index → already +1). Single-pod (ppi==1) counts alive PODS so a
            # within-instance surge — 2 pods at the SAME inst-index on opposite
            # ActiveOrdinal slots (how the controller surges a single-pod
            # Instance, update.go:1262) — is visible. Instance-counting alone
            # collapses both pods into 1 and silently misses the surge.
            agg[c][0] += len(pods) if ppi == 1 else 1
            distinct_alive_idx += 1
            # Per-pod new-revision signal (independent of whole-Instance updated,
            # so a collision that leaves an index half-new is still counted).
            if old_hashes is not None:
                if modes.get(c) == "inplace":
                    idx_new = [q for q in pods if q.get("newanno")]
                else:
                    idx_new = [q for q in pods if q.get("hash") and q["hash"] not in old_hashes]
                new_pods += len(idx_new)
                if idx_new:
                    distinct_new_idx += 1
            ready_pods = sum(1 for q in pods if q["ready"])
            if len(pods) >= ppi and ready_pods >= ppi:
                agg[c][1] += 1  # ready Instance: full pod set, all Ready
                if old_hashes is None:
                    updated = False
                elif modes.get(c) == "inplace":
                    updated = all(q.get("newanno") for q in pods)
                else:
                    updated = all(q.get("hash") and q["hash"] not in old_hashes for q in pods)
                if updated:
                    agg[c][2] += 1
        if measures is not None:
            measures[c] = (distinct_alive_idx, new_pods, distinct_new_idx)
    return {c: tuple(v) for c, v in agg.items()}


def _dump_index_breakdown(ctx, comp, checks):
    """On a collision / shared-index failure, print the settle-snapshot pod
    layout for `comp` (per instance-index: runner:rev:aliveReady) so the log
    proves whether a gang truly settled short (missing/old pod) vs a transient."""
    old = ctx.get("old_hashes") or set()
    by = defaultdict(list)
    for p in (ctx.get("pod_state") or {}).values():
        if p and p.get("comp") == comp:
            by[p.get("inst", "?")].append(p)
    checks.append(f"    · {comp} settle-snapshot per instance-index:")
    for idx in sorted(by, key=lambda x: str(x)):
        parts = [f"{p.get('runner','?')}:{'new' if (p.get('hash') and p['hash'] not in old) else 'old'}:"
                 f"{'A' if p.get('alive') else 'x'}{'R' if p.get('ready') else '-'}" for p in by[idx]]
        checks.append(f"      idx {idx}: {' '.join(parts)}")


def index_collision_checks(ctx, comps, verdict, notes, checks):
    """Distinct-alive-index invariant (fleet-wipe guard). For each Component in
    `comps` assert: (a) the number of instance indices with >=1 alive pod is at
    least the alive Instance count — a shortfall means two DIFFERENT Instances
    (gangs) collapsed onto one index, the collision the Instance-count tuple
    hides; and (b) for gangs (pods_per_inst>1) the raw alive new-revision pod
    count equals distinct_new_index * pods_per_inst — a shortfall means some
    index holds pods from more than one gang (a shared index). Returns the
    (possibly FAIL) verdict; appends to notes/checks in place.

    This is the check that would have caught the 64→1 fleet-wipe: N gangs
    collapsing onto a single index read as one alive Instance to the tuple, but
    distinct-alive-index falls to 1 and the gang pod count no longer matches
    distinct_new_index * pods_per_inst.
    """
    meas = ctx.get("measures") or {}
    agg = ctx.get("agg") or {}
    ppi = ctx["pods_per_inst"]
    for c in comps:
        if ctx["N"].get(c, 0) == 0:
            continue
        distinct_alive, new_pods, distinct_new = meas.get(c, (0, 0, 0))
        alive_inst = agg.get(c, (0, 0, 0))[0]
        _hit = False
        # (a) distinct alive indices must cover the alive Instance count. For a
        # gang (ppi>1) alive_inst is already Instance-counted, so any shortfall
        # is a collision. For single-pod (ppi==1) alive_inst counts PODS (a
        # within-instance surge legitimately puts 2 pods on 1 index), so compare
        # against ceil(alive_inst / ppi_effective) is not meaningful — restrict
        # the distinct-index floor to gangs where the collapse is the failure.
        if ppi.get(c, 1) > 1 and distinct_alive < alive_inst:
            verdict = "FAIL"
            notes.append(f"{c} index collision: {alive_inst} alive Instances on only {distinct_alive} distinct index(es)")
            checks.append(f"  ✗ {c} index collision: {alive_inst} alive Instance(s) share only {distinct_alive} distinct index(es) — gangs collapsed onto one index (fleet-wipe shape)")
            _hit = True
        # (b) gang new-revision pods must partition cleanly across distinct new
        # indices: new_pods == distinct_new * pods_per_inst. A shortfall means an
        # index carries a partial/second gang's pods (shared index).
        if ppi.get(c, 1) > 1 and new_pods and new_pods != distinct_new * ppi[c]:
            verdict = "FAIL"
            notes.append(f"{c} shared index: {new_pods} new pods across {distinct_new} index(es) (want {distinct_new * ppi[c]})")
            checks.append(f"  ✗ {c} shared index: {new_pods} new-revision pod(s) span {distinct_new} distinct index(es) but a clean gang roll needs {distinct_new * ppi[c]} (={distinct_new}×{ppi[c]}) — a new-rev index holds fewer than {ppi[c]} new pods")
            _hit = True
        if _hit:
            _dump_index_breakdown(ctx, c, checks)
    return verdict


def _floor_slack(ctx):
    """Instances the header lets a fault cost below the capacity floor
    (floor_slack=<k>): the gang a podkill takes is not the roll's doing."""
    try:
        return int((ctx.get("hdr") or {}).get("floor_slack") or 0)
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return 0


def _track_gang_and_floor(ctx, comps):
    """Mid-loop bookkeeping shared by the _read_one handlers: (1) per-Instance
    mixed-revision span (gang atomicity), and (2) per-Component min ready
    Instances + below-floor dip span (capacity floor with debounce). Mirrors
    the inline tracking in run_case so _partition/_migrate/_canary get the same
    coverage. Stashes results in ctx: gang_worst, min_ready, floor_sust."""
    now = time.time()
    ppi = ctx["pods_per_inst"]
    modes = ctx["modes"]
    agg = ctx.get("agg") or {}
    gang_mixed_since = ctx.setdefault("gang_mixed_since", {})
    gang_worst = ctx.setdefault("gang_worst", {})
    min_ready = ctx.setdefault("min_ready", {})
    floor_since = ctx.setdefault("floor_since", {})
    floor_sust = ctx.setdefault("floor_sust", {})
    by_comp = defaultdict(lambda: defaultdict(list))
    for q in ctx["pod_state"].values():
        if q and q["alive"]:
            by_comp[q["comp"]][q.get("inst", "0")].append(q)
    for c in comps:
        if ppi.get(c, 1) > 1:
            for inst_idx, ipods in by_comp[c].items():
                if modes.get(c) == "inplace":
                    sigs = {bool(q.get("newanno")) for q in ipods}
                else:
                    sigs = {q.get("hash") for q in ipods if q.get("hash")}
                key = (c, inst_idx)
                if len(sigs) >= 2:                       # mixed old+new within one Instance
                    gang_mixed_since.setdefault(key, now)
                    span = now - gang_mixed_since[key]
                    if span > gang_worst.get(key, 0):
                        gang_worst[key] = span
                else:
                    gang_mixed_since.pop(key, None)
        rd = agg.get(c, (0, 0, 0))[1]
        if c not in min_ready or rd < min_ready[c]:
            min_ready[c] = rd
        # Below-floor dip span → min_ready_checks' FLOOR_SUSTAIN_S debounce
        # (mirrors run_case's Check 10 tracking).
        n = ctx["N"].get(c, 0)
        if n:
            fl = n - resolve_max_unavailable(ctx["info"].get("max_unavail", {}).get(c, 0), n) - _floor_allowance(ctx, c) - _floor_slack(ctx)
            if rd < fl:
                floor_since.setdefault(c, now)
                span = now - floor_since[c]
                if span > floor_sust.get(c, 0.0):
                    floor_sust[c] = span
            else:
                floor_since.pop(c, None)


def gang_atomicity_checks(ctx, comps, verdict, notes, checks):
    """Check 9 ported to the _read_one handlers: each bumped multi-node gang must
    roll leader+workers as ONE unit — no Instance sat mixed-revision >= GANG_TOL_S.
    Requires _track_gang_and_floor to have run over the same comps in the loop."""
    gang_worst = ctx.get("gang_worst") or {}
    mn = [c for c in comps if ctx["pods_per_inst"].get(c, 1) > 1]
    if not mn:
        return verdict
    viol = {k: v for k, v in gang_worst.items() if k[0] in mn and v >= GANG_TOL_S}
    if viol:
        verdict = "FAIL"
        wk = max(viol, key=viol.get)
        notes.append(f"gang atomicity violated: {wk[0]} Instance {wk[1]} mixed-revision {viol[wk]:.0f}s")
        checks.append(f"  ✗ gang atomicity violated: {len(viol)} Instance(s) sat mixed-revision ≥{GANG_TOL_S:.0f}s — leader+workers did NOT roll as a unit (worst {wk[0]} inst {wk[1]}: {viol[wk]:.0f}s)")
    else:
        checks.append(f"  ✓ gang atomicity held: every multi-node Instance ({', '.join(mn)}) rolled leader+workers as a unit")
    return verdict


def surge_before_drain_checks(ctx, comps, verdict, notes, checks):
    """Surge-before-drain ordering for the _read_one handlers: a source pod must
    not begin draining before its Ready surge replacement (drained-old must not
    lead ready-new by more than maxUnavailable). Consumes the running worst breach
    accumulated in _apply_event (ctx['order_viol']). SurgeThenDrain components
    only — RecreatePod also aggregates as mode "surge" but drains first by design,
    and _apply_event only tracks SurgeThenDrain."""
    ov = ctx.get("order_viol") or {}
    surge = [c for c in comps if ctx["info"].get("strat", {}).get(c) == "SurgeThenDrain"]
    if not surge:
        return verdict
    viol = {c: ov.get(c, 0) for c in surge if ov.get(c, 0) > 0}
    if viol and (ctx.get("hdr") or {}).get("order_soft"):
        wc = max(viol, key=viol.get)
        checks.append(f"  ⚠ surge-before-drain: {wc} drained {viol[wc]} pod(s) ahead of ready surges — case opted out (order_soft=1, fault-induced drain); informational")
    elif viol:
        verdict = "FAIL"
        wc = max(viol, key=viol.get)
        notes.append(f"surge-before-drain violated: {wc} drained {viol[wc]} pod(s) ahead of ready surges")
        checks.append(f"  ✗ surge-before-drain violated: {len(viol)} Component(s) began draining a source before its replacement was Ready (worst {wc}: {viol[wc]} pod(s) ahead)")
    else:
        checks.append(f"  ✓ surge-before-drain held: every drain ({', '.join(surge)}) followed a Ready surge replacement")
    return verdict


def min_ready_checks(ctx, comps, verdict, notes, checks, label="capacity floor"):
    """Capacity-floor: each Component's min ready Instances mid-roll stays >=
    N - maxUnavailable. Debounced like run_case's Check 10: only a dip that
    PERSISTED >= FLOOR_SUSTAIN_S fails; shorter dips are reported ⚠ as
    readiness flaps. floor_hard=1 keeps the instantaneous semantics. Requires
    _track_gang_and_floor to have run over `comps`."""
    min_ready = ctx.get("min_ready") or {}
    floor_sust = ctx.get("floor_sust") or {}
    floor_hard = bool((ctx.get("hdr") or {}).get("floor_hard"))
    floor_soft = bool((ctx.get("hdr") or {}).get("floor_soft"))
    mu = ctx["info"].get("max_unavail", {})
    slack = _floor_slack(ctx)
    for c in comps:
        if ctx["N"].get(c, 0) == 0:
            continue
        broken = _floor_allowance(ctx, c)
        floor = ctx["N"][c] - resolve_max_unavailable(mu.get(c, 0), ctx["N"][c]) - broken - slack
        basis = "N-maxUnavailable" + (f"-{broken}broken" if broken else "") + (f"-{slack}slack" if slack else "")
        mr = min_ready.get(c, ctx["N"][c])
        sust = floor_sust.get(c, 0.0)
        if mr >= floor:
            checks.append(f"  ✓ {c} {label} held: min ready {mr} ≥ {basis}={floor}")
        elif floor_soft:
            checks.append(f"  ⚠ {c} capacity dipped to {mr} ready Instance(s) (< {basis}={floor}) — case opted out (floor_soft=1); informational")
        elif floor_hard or sust >= FLOOR_SUSTAIN_S:
            verdict = "FAIL"
            held = "" if floor_hard else f", dip held {sust:.0f}s ≥ {FLOOR_SUSTAIN_S:.0f}s"
            notes.append(f"{c} {label} breached: min ready {mr} < {basis}={floor}")
            checks.append(f"  ✗ {c} {label} breached: min ready {mr} < {basis}={floor}{held} — did NOT preserve capacity")
        else:
            checks.append(f"  ⚠ {c} capacity dipped to {mr} ready Instance(s) (< {basis}={floor}) for <{FLOOR_SUSTAIN_S:.0f}s — debounced as a readiness flap (not failed)")
    return verdict


def _floor_allowance(ctx, comp):
    """Instances of comp the case itself broke (a break fault's victims):
    their capacity is the fault's cost, so the floor the healthy Instances
    must hold is lowered by that many."""
    return int((ctx.get("floor_allowance") or {}).get(comp, 0))


def fetch_status(case_id):
    r = kubectl("-n", NS, "get", "isvc", case_id, "-o", "json")
    if r.returncode != 0:
        return {}
    try:
        return json.loads(r.stdout).get("status", {})
    except Exception:
        return {}


def fetch_rev_services(case_id):
    r = kubectl("-n", NS, "get", "svc", "-l", f"ome.io/inferenceservice={case_id}",
                "-o", "json")
    if r.returncode != 0:
        return []
    try:
        return [i["metadata"]["name"] for i in json.loads(r.stdout).get("items", [])]
    except Exception:
        return []


def _teardown_survivors(case_id):
    """Live leftovers for a case after its delete: [(kind, name, node)] across
    component pods, InferenceReplicas, Services (incl. per-revision), and the
    ISVC object itself. Empty = teardown converged. A missing CRD or NotFound
    reads as gone (version-tolerant: pre-IR builds have no inferencereplicas)."""
    sel = f"ome.io/inferenceservice={case_id}"
    left = []
    for kind, res in (("pod", "pod"), ("inferencereplica", "inferencereplicas"), ("svc", "svc")):
        r = kubectl("-n", NS, "get", res, "-l", sel, "-o", "json")
        if r.returncode != 0:
            continue
        try:
            items = json.loads(r.stdout).get("items", [])
        except Exception:
            continue
        for it in items:
            node = (it.get("spec") or {}).get("nodeName", "") if kind == "pod" else ""
            left.append((kind, (it.get("metadata") or {}).get("name", "?"), node))
    if kubectl("-n", NS, "get", "isvc", case_id, "-o", "name").returncode == 0:
        left.append(("isvc", case_id, ""))
    return left


def teardown_check(case_id, total_pods, verdict, notes, checks):
    """Universal end-of-case teardown gate: after the case's delete, poll
    (bounded) until zero component pods, no InferenceReplicas, no Services and
    no ISVC remain. Anything surviving the budget FAILs the verdict, naming
    each survivor (kind/name/node) — a cleanup that doesn't converge is a
    controller bug (wedged finalizer / orphaned pods), not a mop-up detail."""
    budget = min(MAX_BUDGET_S, TEARDOWN_BASE_S + TEARDOWN_PER_POD_S * max(0, total_pods))
    deadline = time.time() + budget
    left = _teardown_survivors(case_id)
    while left and time.time() < deadline:
        time.sleep(TEARDOWN_POLL_S)
        left = _teardown_survivors(case_id)
    if left:
        named = ", ".join(f"{k}/{n}" + (f"@{node}" if node else "") for k, n, node in left[:8])
        more = f" (+{len(left) - 8} more)" if len(left) > 8 else ""
        verdict = "FAIL"
        notes.append(f"teardown did not converge in {budget}s: {named}{more}")
        checks.append(f"  ✗ teardown did not converge within {budget}s — survivors: {named}{more}")
    else:
        checks.append("  ✓ teardown converged: pods, InferenceReplicas, Services, ISVC all gone")
    return verdict


# ── Continuous invariants ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Invariants the pod-observed verdicts are blind to, polled every INV_TICK_S
# for the whole case:
#   A status-truth      — an IR Instance must not claim Phase=Failed while its
#                         full pod set is Ready+serving, nor Phase=Ready with
#                         zero pods for its index.
#   B endpoints-membership — every Ready+serving pod that revision-matches a
#                         per-revision routed Service must be a Ready endpoint
#                         of it, and no endpoint may reference a deleted pod.
#   C pair-alive        — during a non-empty→non-empty pairing-protocol
#                         transition (armed only by mode=pairing), whenever
#                         both engine and decoder serve, a pairable pair must
#                         exist; the gate's no-pair and 1×1-wall escapes are
#                         exempt.
#   F label-truth       — every live pod runs the template its revision-hash
#                         label names: images, the trigger annotation, literal
#                         env and requests match the ControllerRevision of
#                         that hash (or, until one is visible, the first pod
#                         seen under the hash).
#   G ready-serving     — an Instance the IR reports Ready, whose full pod set
#                         the watcher sees Ready, has a pod in rotation: the
#                         serving gate True and a Ready endpoint of a routed
#                         Service that selects it.
#   H superseded-revision — once a Component's rollout reports done (run closed
#                         Completed with the phase at Stable, or for a Component
#                         outside the run model the IR's currentRevision at
#                         updateRevision), every Instance row and every live pod
#                         is on that revision. Not evaluated under mode=partition,
#                         whose verdict owns the staged split.
# A violation must hold for its sustain count of CONSECUTIVE ticks to fire
# (see the INV_* constants for the carve-out arithmetic); fired violations
# dedup per (invariant, kind, subject) with first/last timestamps and an
# occurrence count, and FAIL the verdict via invariant_checks.


def _pod_serving(obj):
    """True when the pod's ome.io/serving readiness-gate condition is True."""
    for c in (obj.get("status", {}).get("conditions") or []):
        if c.get("type") == SERVING_COND:
            return c.get("status") == "True"
    return False


def _pod_placement(obj, labels):
    """Scheduler-facing fields every watcher record carries, whichever loop
    builds it: node binding, scheduler name, the pod-group label and the
    nodes a required hostname NotIn term keeps the pod off. Invariant D
    reads the first three, invariant K the last; a record without them is
    never evaluated."""
    spec = obj.get("spec") or {}
    return {
        "node": spec.get("nodeName", ""),
        "sched": spec.get("schedulerName", ""),
        "pg": labels.get("scheduling.x-k8s.io/pod-group", ""),
        "excl": _hostname_exclusions(spec),
    }


def _hostname_exclusions(spec):
    """The node names a pod's required node affinity keeps it off: every
    value of a kubernetes.io/hostname NotIn term, sorted."""
    required = (((spec.get("affinity") or {}).get("nodeAffinity") or {})
                .get("requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution") or {})
    out = set()
    for term in required.get("nodeSelectorTerms") or []:
        for expr in term.get("matchExpressions") or []:
            if expr.get("key") == HOSTNAME_LABEL and expr.get("operator") == "NotIn":
                out.update(str(v) for v in expr.get("values") or [])
    return sorted(out)


def _pod_template(obj):
    """Template-derived field every watcher record carries, whichever loop
    builds it: the fingerprint of what the pod actually runs. Invariant F
    compares it with the template the pod's revision-hash label names; a
    record without it is never evaluated."""
    meta = obj.get("metadata") or {}
    return {"tmpl": _template_fingerprint(obj.get("spec") or {}, meta.get("annotations") or {})}


def _template_fingerprint(pod_spec, annotations):
    """The parts of a pod template a revision pins and a rendered pod keeps
    verbatim: every container's image, the rollout trigger annotation, each
    container's literal env values and resource requests. Env the renderer
    owns (OME_*) and anything admission adds are outside the comparison,
    which reads template-is-a-subset-of-pod. An unnamed template container
    is the main container, which is what the renderer names it."""
    images, env, requests = {}, {}, {}
    for ctn in list(pod_spec.get("initContainers") or []) + list(pod_spec.get("containers") or []):
        name = ctn.get("name") or MAIN_CONTAINER
        images[name] = ctn.get("image") or ""
        env[name] = {e["name"]: str(e.get("value", "")) for e in (ctn.get("env") or [])
                     if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get("name") and "valueFrom" not in e
                     and not str(e["name"]).startswith("OME_")}
        reqs = {}
        for res, val in (((ctn.get("resources") or {}).get("requests")) or {}).items():
            try:
                reqs[res] = _qty(res, val)
            except (TypeError, ValueError):
                continue
        requests[name] = reqs
    return {"images": images, "anno": str(annotations.get(TRIGGER_ANNO, "") or ""),
            "env": env, "requests": requests}


def _template_mismatch(expected, actual):
    """Where a rendered pod departs from its revision's template, as
    'field: revision value vs pod value' lines; empty when the pod runs the
    template. Only the template's own entries are compared."""
    diffs = []
    if expected["anno"] != actual["anno"]:
        diffs.append(f"annotation {TRIGGER_ANNO}: revision {expected['anno']!r} vs pod {actual['anno']!r}")
    for name, image in expected["images"].items():
        got = actual["images"].get(name)
        if got is None:
            diffs.append(f"container {name}: in the revision, not on the pod")
        elif got != image:
            diffs.append(f"container {name} image: revision {image!r} vs pod {got!r}")
    for name, env in expected["env"].items():
        pod_env = actual["env"].get(name) or {}
        for var, val in env.items():
            if pod_env.get(var) != val:
                diffs.append(f"container {name} env {var}: revision {val!r} vs pod {pod_env.get(var)!r}")
    for name, reqs in expected["requests"].items():
        pod_reqs = actual["requests"].get(name) or {}
        for res, val in reqs.items():
            if pod_reqs.get(res) != val:
                diffs.append(f"container {name} requests.{res}: revision {val} vs pod {pod_reqs.get(res)}")
    return diffs


def _rev_hash(name):
    """The hash segment of a revision reference — a ControllerRevision name
    (`<isvc>-<component>-<hash>`) or an already bare hash."""
    return (name or "").rsplit("-", 1)[-1]


def _pod_role(p):
    """Which stored template a pod renders from: workers the worker template,
    every other runner the pod template."""
    return "worker" if p.get("runner") == "worker" else "pod"


def _pod_mutated_by_harness(inv, name, uid):
    """Record a live pod whose spec the harness changed itself, so invariant F
    never judges that UID against its revision. Every verb that patches a
    live pod's spec calls this; deletions need no record, the pod leaves the
    live set and its replacement is a new UID."""
    if inv is not None and uid:
        inv["mutated_uids"][uid] = name


def _inv_new(case_id, hdr):
    """Fresh invariant-poller state. Header `inv_off=<class>|all` over
    INV_CLASSES (which requires an adjacent '# reason:' comment — enforced by
    validate-only) disables checks.
    Invariant C (pair-alive) additionally requires arming: a pairing-mode
    handler sets inv["pairing"] at trigger time for a non-empty→non-empty
    protocol transition; without that it never evaluates."""
    off = str(hdr.get("inv_off", "") or "")
    opted = {c for c in str(hdr.get("inv_on", "") or "").split(",") if c}
    return {
        "case_id": case_id,
        "off": off,
        "a_on": off not in ("A", "all"),
        "b_on": off not in ("B", "all"),
        "c_on": off not in ("C", "all"),
        # Invariant F (label truth): (hash, role) → {"fp": template fingerprint,
        # "src": "revision" | "first pod <name>"}, and per hash how many
        # ControllerRevision lists lacked it (re-listing is bounded).
        "f_on": off not in ("F", "all"),
        "f_seen": False,        # ≥1 pod compared against its revision's template
        "revisions": {},
        "rev_tries": {},
        # Invariant G (ready implies serving).
        "g_on": off not in ("G", "all"),
        "g_seen": False,          # ≥1 Ready Instance with its pod set Ready was evaluated
        "g_routing_seen": False,  # ≥1 routed Service observed: the endpoint half asserted
        # Invariant H (no superseded revision once the rollout reports done).
        # The partition verb's verdict owns its staged split — k Instances
        # rest on the old revision by design — so H is not evaluated there.
        "h_on": off not in ("H", "all") and str(hdr.get("mode") or "") != "partition",
        "h_seen": False,          # ≥1 Component reporting its rollout done was evaluated
        # Invariants J (no auto-recovery record in the audit ledger) and K (no
        # required hostname NotIn term on a live pod) are opt-in: inv_on=.
        "j_on": "J" in opted and off not in ("J", "all"),
        "j_seen": False,          # the audit ledger was read at least once
        "k_on": "K" in opted and off not in ("K", "all"),
        "k_seen": False,          # ≥1 live pod's node affinity was read
        # Invariant D (gang scheduling) exists only when the fixtures name a
        # scheduler (OME_EVAL_SCHEDULER): every pod must run under it and every
        # gang must bind as one PodGroup.
        "d_on": bool(SCHED_NAME) and off not in ("D", "all"),
        "d_seen": False,        # invariant D observed at least one live pod
        "pg_seen": False,       # invariant D resolved at least one PodGroup
        "pg_unavailable": False,  # PodGroup API missing: D2 skipped, D1/D3 still assert
        # inv_xfail scope: a violation of this invariant class is the case's
        # tracked bug (notimpl issue) and records as the XFAIL, never a FAIL.
        "xfail": str(hdr.get("inv_xfail", "") or ""),
        "xfail_issue": hdr.get("issue"),
        "last": 0.0,        # last tick timestamp (self-rate-limited)
        "streaks": {},      # streak_key → consecutive-tick observation count
        "viol": {},         # viol_key → {first, last, n, detail}
        "ir_seen": False,   # instanceStatuses observed at least once (version tolerance)
        # (comp, source, replacement, source revision) for every gang surge
        # the status rows were seen to claim, oldest claim first.
        "surges": [],
        "b_seen": False,    # invariant B evaluated ≥1 Ready+serving pod against a routed Service
        "dead_uids": set(), # pod UIDs whose DELETED watch event was observed
        # uid → pod name of the live pods whose spec the harness changed itself
        # (a break pointing a pod at another image). Invariant F does not judge
        # them; a replacement the engine builds is a new UID and is judged.
        "mutated_uids": {},
        # Set by the pairing handler for a non-empty→non-empty transition:
        # {"frm": F, "to": T, "armed": bool, "seen": bool}. armed flips True on
        # every pairable sample and gates the violation — once the pair is gone
        # (for any reason) the unpaired samples that follow are the product
        # legitimately progressing back toward a pair, not the gate breaking one.
        "pairing": None,
        # Set by the canary handler when both pairing Components stage: the
        # cohort-ratio observer (invariant E), informational until the
        # contract is decided.
        "ratio": None,
    }


def _instance_rows(ir_status):
    """Decoded per-Instance rows of an InferenceReplica status for a case
    log; none when the status carries no rows or does not decode."""
    try:
        return irstatus.instance_statuses(ir_status) or []
    except irstatus.DecodeError:
        return []


def _inv_hit(inv, hits, streak_key, viol_key, sustain, now, detail):
    """One tick's observation of a violating condition. Fires (records a
    violation) only once the streak reaches `sustain` consecutive ticks."""
    hits.add(streak_key)
    n = inv["streaks"].get(streak_key, 0) + 1
    inv["streaks"][streak_key] = n
    if n < sustain:
        return
    v = inv["viol"].get(viol_key)
    if v is None:
        inv["viol"][viol_key] = {"first": now, "last": now, "n": 1, "detail": detail}
        print(f"    ✗ INVARIANT {viol_key[0]} ({viol_key[1]}): {detail}")
    else:
        v["last"] = now
        v["n"] += 1
        v["detail"] = detail


def _note_gang_surges(inv, comp, rows):
    """Keep inv["surges"] current with one tick's rows of a Component: the
    gang surge pairs (comp, source, replacement, source revision) the rows
    claim, oldest claim first. A source row names its replacement index
    from the claim until the row's removal, so a tick anywhere in that
    window records the pair whether or not the ISVC events kept the start.
    The source seen again on its running revision without that claim was
    reset (the surge abandoned, or retried at another index) and its pair
    goes; its index gone, or held by a row on another revision, is the
    surge complete."""
    pairs = inv.setdefault("surges", [])
    by_index = {str(r.get("index")): r for r in rows}
    claims = {}
    for idx, r in by_index.items():
        op = r.get("operation") or {}
        if op.get("type") == "Update" and op.get("surgeIndex") is not None:
            claims[idx] = str(op["surgeIndex"])

    def reset(pair):
        c, src, dst, rev = pair
        row = by_index.get(src)
        return c == comp and row is not None and row.get("runningRevision") == rev and claims.get(src) != dst

    pairs[:] = [pair for pair in pairs if not reset(pair)]
    for src, dst in claims.items():
        pair = (comp, src, dst, by_index[src].get("runningRevision"))
        if pair not in pairs:
            pairs.append(pair)


def _inv_check_status_truth(inv, pod_state, pods_per_inst, ir_items, hits, now):
    """Invariant A, one tick: compare each IR Instance's claimed phase against
    the watcher's live pods for its index. Version-tolerant: a build without
    the IR CRD / instanceStatuses field leaves ir_seen False and the verdict
    prints one ⓘ note instead of asserting."""
    if ir_items is None:
        return
    existing = defaultdict(list)   # (comp, inst-index) → pod records still existing
    for p in pod_state.values():
        if p:
            existing[(p["comp"], p.get("inst", "0"))].append(p)
    for it in ir_items:
        comp = (it.get("spec") or {}).get("component", "?")
        try:
            insts = irstatus.instance_statuses(it.get("status") or {})
        except irstatus.DecodeError as e:
            key = ("A", "undecodable-status", comp, "-")
            _inv_hit(inv, hits, key, key, INV_SUSTAIN_A, now,
                     f"{comp}: per-Instance status undecodable: {e}")
            continue
        if insts is None:
            continue   # pre-IR-status build — field absent
        inv["ir_seen"] = True
        _note_gang_surges(inv, comp, insts)
        ppi = max(1, pods_per_inst.get(comp, 1))
        for ist in insts:
            phase = ist.get("phase")
            idx = str(ist.get("index", "?"))
            if phase in INV_TRANSIENT_PHASES:
                continue   # transitional phases are exempt from all A-checks
            pods = existing.get((comp, idx), [])
            if phase == "Failed":
                # Failed-while-serving: the Instance claims Failed while its
                # FULL pod set is alive, Ready and in the serving rotation.
                alive = [p for p in pods if p["alive"]]
                if len(alive) >= ppi and all(p["ready"] and p.get("serving") for p in alive):
                    key = ("A", "failed-while-serving", comp, idx)
                    _inv_hit(inv, hits, key, key, INV_SUSTAIN_A, now,
                             f"{comp}/{idx} Phase=Failed while all {len(alive)} live pod(s) are Ready+serving")
            elif phase == "Ready":
                # Ready-without-pods reads the IR's own podCount, not
                # the watcher's separately-collected pod_state. The two are
                # independent data sources with independent lag: under slow
                # concurrent scheduling the watcher's pod stream trails the IR,
                # so comparing IR-phase against watcher-pods fires "Ready but I
                # see no pod" for indices whose pod exists from the apiserver's
                # view — a harness split-brain, not a product lie.
                if int(ist.get("podCount", 0)) == 0:
                    key = ("A", "ready-without-pods", comp, idx)
                    _inv_hit(inv, hits, key, key, INV_SUSTAIN_A, now,
                             f"{comp}/{idx} Phase=Ready while the IR's own podCount is 0")


# Selector keys the watcher can evaluate against its pod records. Keys every
# OMENative-managed pod carries by construction (the watcher's own selector /
# the managed-by stamp) are treated as always-matching.
_INV_SEL_KEYS = ("component", REV_LABEL, "ome.io/runner", "ome.io/pod-ordinal")
_INV_SEL_UNIVERSAL = {"ome.io/inferenceservice", "ome.io/managed-by"}


def _inv_fetch_routing(case_id):
    """(Services, EndpointSlices) of the case; None when either list cannot be read."""
    sel = f"ome.io/inferenceservice={case_id}"
    rs = kubectl("-n", NS, "get", "svc", "-l", sel, "-o", "json")
    re_ = kubectl("-n", NS, "get", "endpointslices", "-l", sel, "-o", "json")
    if rs.returncode != 0 or re_.returncode != 0:
        return None
    try:
        return json.loads(rs.stdout).get("items", []), json.loads(re_.stdout).get("items", [])
    except Exception:
        return None


def _routed_services(routing):
    """The per-revision ROUTED Services the watcher can evaluate, as
    [(name, selector, ready_uids, all_uids)]: the selector carries the
    revision-hash label and only labels the records track; headless peer-DNS
    Services are excluded (they publish not-ready addresses by design).
    Endpoints are merged across a Service's slices; the EndpointConditions
    contract reads a nil ready as ready."""
    svcs, slices = routing
    eps = defaultdict(list)   # service name → endpoints (slices merged; labels are service-mirrored)
    for sl in slices:
        svc_name = ((sl.get("metadata") or {}).get("labels") or {}).get("kubernetes.io/service-name")
        if svc_name:
            eps[svc_name].extend(sl.get("endpoints") or [])
    out = []
    for s in svcs:
        spec = s.get("spec") or {}
        selector = spec.get("selector") or {}
        name = ((s.get("metadata") or {}).get("name")) or "?"
        if spec.get("clusterIP") == "None" or REV_LABEL not in selector:
            continue   # headless (peer DNS) or not a per-revision routed Service
        if set(selector) - set(_INV_SEL_KEYS) - _INV_SEL_UNIVERSAL:
            continue   # selector uses a label the watcher doesn't track — can't evaluate
        ready_uids, all_uids = set(), set()
        for ep in eps.get(name, []):
            u = (ep.get("targetRef") or {}).get("uid")
            if not u:
                continue
            all_uids.add(u)
            if (ep.get("conditions") or {}).get("ready") is not False:
                ready_uids.add(u)
        out.append((name, selector, ready_uids, all_uids))
    return out


def _pod_selected(p, selector):
    """True when a routed Service's selector matches the watcher record."""
    view = {"component": p["comp"], REV_LABEL: p.get("hash", ""),
            "ome.io/runner": p.get("runner", "default"),
            "ome.io/pod-ordinal": p.get("ord", "0")}
    return not any(k in selector and view[k] != selector[k] for k in _INV_SEL_KEYS)


def _inv_check_endpoints(inv, pod_state, routing, hits, now):
    """Invariant B, one tick: for each per-revision ROUTED Service, every
    alive+Ready+serving pod matching the selector must appear as a Ready
    endpoint, and no endpoint may reference a pod UID whose DELETED event the
    watcher has seen."""
    if routing is None:
        return
    for name, selector, ready_uids, all_uids in _routed_services(routing):
        for pname, p in pod_state.items():
            if not p or not p["alive"] or not p["ready"] or not p.get("serving") or not p.get("uid"):
                continue
            if not _pod_selected(p, selector):
                continue   # pod is not a member of this Service
            inv["b_seen"] = True   # membership actually evaluated (non-vacuous)
            if p["uid"] not in ready_uids:
                _inv_hit(inv, hits, ("B", "missing-endpoint", name, pname), ("B", "missing-endpoint", name),
                         INV_SUSTAIN_B_MISSING, now,
                         f"svc {name}: pod {pname} is Ready+serving on its revision but absent from the Ready endpoints")
        for u in all_uids & inv["dead_uids"]:
            _inv_hit(inv, hits, ("B", "stale-endpoint", name, u), ("B", "stale-endpoint", name),
                     INV_SUSTAIN_B_STALE, now,
                     f"svc {name}: endpoint still references deleted pod UID {u[:13]}…")


def _pairing_serving_split(pod_state):
    """(engine_insts, decoder_insts): serving Instances per pairing Component,
    each a list of the instance's serving pods' pairing-protocol labels. An
    Instance is serving when >=1 of its pods is alive+Ready+serving (mirrors
    the gate's ServingPodCount>0)."""
    by = {"engine": defaultdict(list), "decoder": defaultdict(list)}
    for p in pod_state.values():
        if p and p["alive"] and p["ready"] and p.get("serving") and p["comp"] in by:
            by[p["comp"]][p.get("inst", "0")].append(p.get("pairing", ""))
    return list(by["engine"].values()), list(by["decoder"].values())


def _inv_check_pair_alive(inv, pod_state, hits, now):
    """Invariant C, one tick: during a non-empty→non-empty pairing-protocol
    transition, whenever both engine and decoder have >=1 serving Instance a
    pairable pair must exist — some serving engine pod and serving decoder pod
    with equal protocols, or either empty (empty pairs with anything).

    The gate's liveness escapes are exempt where the window is unavoidable:
      - no pair to protect: once no pairable pair exists (a side at zero, or
        externally destroyed), the check DISARMS — the unpaired samples that
        follow are the product progressing back toward a pair, exactly what the
        no-pair-pre-existing escape allows. It re-arms on the next pairable
        sample. The last-hop escape's window is covered by the same rule: the
        acting side's final hop passes through zero serving, which disarms.
      - the 1×1 mutual wall, for drain-first strategies only: with nothing
        able to come up before something goes down, the first-mover window is
        unavoidable. Under a surge or in-place strategy both replacements come
        up regardless, so the old pair can keep serving until the new pair
        exists, and an unpaired sample at 1×1 is a violation.
    """
    st = inv.get("pairing")
    if not st:
        return
    eng, dec = _pairing_serving_split(pod_state)
    if not eng or not dec:
        st["armed"] = False   # a side has nothing serving — no pair to protect
        return
    st["seen"] = True
    pairable = any(pe == "" or pd == "" or pe == pd
                   for insts_e in eng for pe in insts_e
                   for insts_d in dec for pd in insts_d)
    if pairable:
        st["armed"] = True
        return
    if len(eng) <= 1 and len(dec) <= 1 and st.get("drain_first"):
        return   # 1×1 mutual wall under drain-first: unavoidable window; stays armed
    if not st["armed"]:
        return
    key = ("C", "pair-alive")
    eng_p = sorted({pe for insts in eng for pe in insts})
    dec_p = sorted({pd for insts in dec for pd in insts})
    _inv_hit(inv, hits, key, key, INV_SUSTAIN_C, now,
             f"no pairable serving engine+decoder pair during {st['frm']!r}→{st['to']!r} "
             f"(engine serves {eng_p}, decoder serves {dec_p})")


INV_SUSTAIN_E = 2    # cohort-ratio ticks (10 s): a skew this long is not a startup transient


def _cohort_serving_instances(pod_state, pods_per_inst, old_hashes):
    """{component: (new, old)} fully serving Instance counts by revision
    cohort: an Instance counts when every one of its pods is alive+Ready+serving
    and all of them agree on the cohort (a mixed Instance counts as neither)."""
    by = defaultdict(list)
    for p in pod_state.values():
        if p and p.get("alive"):
            by[(p.get("comp"), p.get("inst", "0"))].append(p)
    out = {}
    for (comp, _), pods in by.items():
        expected = max(1, pods_per_inst.get(comp, 1))
        if len(pods) < expected or sum(1 for p in pods if p.get("ready") and p.get("serving")) < expected:
            continue
        cohorts = {bool(p.get("hash") and p["hash"] not in old_hashes) for p in pods}
        new, old = out.get(comp, (0, 0))
        if cohorts == {True}:
            out[comp] = (new + 1, old)
        elif cohorts == {False}:
            out[comp] = (new, old + 1)
    return out


def _inv_check_cohort_ratio(inv, pod_state, pods_per_inst, now):
    """Invariant E, one tick, informational: while a canary stages both pairing
    Components, the canary cohort's engine:decoder serving ratio, read whenever
    both sides have any canary capacity, should stay within the tolerance of
    the fleet's ratio. The executor holds the ratio only at the traffic shift
    today, so a sustained skew is recorded and reported, never failed, until
    the contract is decided."""
    st = inv.get("ratio")
    if not st:
        return
    cohorts = _cohort_serving_instances(pod_state, pods_per_inst, st["old_hashes"])
    ne, nd = cohorts.get("engine", (0, 0))[0], cohorts.get("decoder", (0, 0))[0]
    if ne == 0 or nd == 0:
        st["streak"] = 0
        return
    st["samples"] += 1
    fleet = st["N"]["engine"] / st["N"]["decoder"]
    dev = abs((ne / nd) / fleet - 1.0)
    if dev <= st["tol"]:
        st["streak"] = 0
        return
    st["streak"] += 1
    if st["streak"] < INV_SUSTAIN_E:
        return
    if st["streak"] == INV_SUSTAIN_E:
        st["excursions"] += 1
    if dev > st["worst"]:
        st["worst"] = dev
        st["worst_detail"] = (f"canary cohort serves engine {ne} : decoder {nd} against a fleet of "
                              f"{st['N']['engine']} : {st['N']['decoder']}")


def _inv_fetch_ir_items(case_id):
    """The case's InferenceReplica objects; None when the list cannot be read."""
    return _fetch_initial_ir_items(case_id)


def _inv_fetch_revisions(case_id):
    """revision hash → stored template payload (podSpec, podMeta,
    workerPodSpec) of the case's ControllerRevisions; None when the list
    cannot be read."""
    r = kubectl("-n", NS, "get", "controllerrevisions", "-l",
                f"ome.io/inferenceservice={case_id}", "-o", "json")
    if r.returncode != 0:
        return None
    try:
        items = json.loads(r.stdout).get("items", [])
    except Exception:
        return None
    out = {}
    for it in items:
        name = (it.get("metadata") or {}).get("name") or ""
        data = it.get("data")
        if name and isinstance(data, dict):
            out[_rev_hash(name)] = data
    return out


def _revision_template(payload, role):
    """Fingerprint of a stored revision for one pod role: workers render from
    workerPodSpec when the revision carries one, every other runner from
    podSpec; both share podMeta's annotations."""
    spec = payload.get("podSpec") or {}
    if role == "worker" and isinstance(payload.get("workerPodSpec"), dict):
        spec = payload["workerPodSpec"]
    annos = ((payload.get("podMeta") or {}).get("annotations")) or {}
    return _template_fingerprint(spec, annos)


def _inv_revisions_wanted(inv, pod_state):
    """True while a live pod carries a revision hash the ledger has not read
    off a ControllerRevision and that hash's re-list budget remains."""
    for p in pod_state.values():
        if not p or not p["alive"] or not p.get("hash") or "tmpl" not in p:
            continue
        entry = inv["revisions"].get((p["hash"], _pod_role(p)))
        if (entry is None or entry["src"] != "revision") \
                and inv["rev_tries"].get(p["hash"], 0) < INV_SUSTAIN_SETTLE:
            return True
    return False


def _inv_learn_revisions(inv, pod_state, revisions):
    """Fold a ControllerRevision list into the ledger: every (hash, role) a
    live pod needs reads its template off the stored revision, replacing a
    first-pod stand-in; a hash absent from the list spends one attempt."""
    for p in pod_state.values():
        if not p or not p["alive"] or not p.get("hash") or "tmpl" not in p:
            continue
        key = (p["hash"], _pod_role(p))
        entry = inv["revisions"].get(key)
        if entry is not None and entry["src"] == "revision":
            continue
        payload = revisions.get(p["hash"])
        if payload is None:
            inv["rev_tries"][p["hash"]] = inv["rev_tries"].get(p["hash"], 0) + 1
            continue
        inv["revisions"][key] = {"fp": _revision_template(payload, key[1]), "src": "revision"}


def _inv_check_label_truth(inv, pod_state, hits, now):
    """Invariant F, one tick: every live pod runs the template its
    revision-hash label names. The template is the ControllerRevision of that
    hash; until one is visible (or when none exists) the first pod seen under
    the hash stands in, so a pod rebuilt from a newer template under an old
    label still disagrees with the pods that carried the label first."""
    for pname, p in sorted(pod_state.items()):
        if not p or not p["alive"] or not p.get("hash") or "tmpl" not in p:
            continue
        if p.get("uid") in inv["mutated_uids"]:
            continue   # the harness changed this pod's spec itself
        key = (p["hash"], _pod_role(p))
        entry = inv["revisions"].get(key)
        if entry is None:
            inv["revisions"][key] = {"fp": p["tmpl"], "src": f"first pod {pname}"}
            continue
        inv["f_seen"] = True
        diffs = _template_mismatch(entry["fp"], p["tmpl"])
        if not diffs:
            continue
        source = ("its ControllerRevision" if entry["src"] == "revision"
                  else f"the template the {entry['src']} ran under that label")
        key = ("F", "label-template-mismatch", p["comp"], pname)
        _inv_hit(inv, hits, key, key, INV_SUSTAIN_SETTLE, now,
                 f"{p['comp']}/{p.get('inst', '0')} pod {pname} carries {REV_LABEL}={p['hash']} "
                 f"but runs a different template from {source}: " + "; ".join(diffs[:3]))


def _rotation_uids(routing, pod_state):
    """UIDs of the pods in rotation — Ready endpoints of a routed Service
    whose selector matches them. None when no routed Service is visible at
    all (a build without per-revision routing cannot assert membership)."""
    routed = _routed_services(routing) if routing is not None else []
    if not routed:
        return None
    uids = set()
    for _name, selector, ready_uids, _all in routed:
        for p in pod_state.values():
            if p and p.get("uid") in ready_uids and _pod_selected(p, selector):
                uids.add(p["uid"])
    return uids


def _inv_check_ready_serving(inv, pod_state, pods_per_inst, ir_items, routing, hits, now):
    """Invariant G, one tick: an Instance the IR reports Ready, whose full pod
    set the watcher sees Ready, has at least one pod in rotation — the serving
    gate True and a Ready endpoint of a routed Service that selects it. The
    endpoint half is asserted only once a routed Service is visible; the
    gate half always. An Instance whose pod set is incomplete or not all
    Ready is some other invariant's business."""
    if ir_items is None:
        return
    in_rotation = _rotation_uids(routing, pod_state)
    if in_rotation is not None:
        inv["g_routing_seen"] = True
    existing = defaultdict(list)   # (comp, inst-index) → [(name, live record)]
    for pname, p in sorted(pod_state.items()):
        if p and p["alive"]:
            existing[(p["comp"], p.get("inst", "0"))].append((pname, p))
    for it in ir_items:
        comp = (it.get("spec") or {}).get("component", "?")
        try:
            rows = irstatus.instance_statuses(it.get("status") or {})
        except irstatus.DecodeError:
            continue   # invariant A reports an undecodable status
        ppi = max(1, pods_per_inst.get(comp, 1))
        for row in rows or []:
            if row.get("phase") != "Ready":
                continue
            idx = str(row.get("index", "?"))
            pods = existing.get((comp, idx), [])
            if len(pods) < ppi or not all(p["ready"] for _n, p in pods):
                continue
            inv["g_seen"] = True
            serving = [(n, p) for n, p in pods if p.get("serving")]
            if not serving:
                detail = (f"{comp}/{idx} Phase=Ready with all {len(pods)} pod(s) Ready, "
                          f"but no pod has the {SERVING_COND} gate True")
            elif in_rotation is not None and not any(p.get("uid") in in_rotation for _n, p in serving):
                names = ", ".join(n for n, _p in serving)
                detail = (f"{comp}/{idx} Phase=Ready, pod(s) {names} serving but not a Ready "
                          f"endpoint of any routed Service that selects them")
            else:
                continue
            key = ("G", "ready-not-serving", comp, idx)
            _inv_hit(inv, hits, key, key, INV_SUSTAIN_SETTLE, now, detail)


def _rollout_done_target(comp, ir_status, isvc_status):
    """The revision every Instance of comp must run once its rollout reports
    done, or None while it does not. A Component the ISVC run model pins is
    done when no run is open, the last run closed Completed, its
    rolloutPhase (where a canary reports one) is Stable and the IR's
    updateRevision is the run's pinned target; any other Component is done
    when the IR's own currentRevision has reached updateRevision."""
    update = ir_status.get("updateRevision") or ""
    if not update:
        return None
    rollout = (isvc_status or {}).get("rollout") or {}
    active = rollout.get("activeRun")
    last = rollout.get("lastRun") or {}
    pinned = {}
    for run_record in (active or {}, last):
        for target in (run_record.get("targetRevisions") or []):
            if isinstance(target, dict) and target.get("component") == comp:
                pinned.setdefault(comp, target.get("revision") or "")
    if comp in pinned:
        if active is not None or last.get("outcome") != "Completed":
            return None
        phase = (((isvc_status or {}).get("components") or {}).get(comp) or {}).get("rolloutPhase")
        if phase and phase != "Stable":
            return None
        if _rev_hash(pinned[comp]) != _rev_hash(update):
            return None   # the run record and the IR name different targets: between runs
        return update
    if (ir_status.get("currentRevision") or "") != update:
        return None
    return update


def _inv_check_superseded(inv, pod_state, ir_items, isvc_status, hits, now):
    """Invariant H, one tick: once a Component's rollout reports done, every
    IR row (runningRevision) and every live pod (revision-hash label) of that
    Component is on the revision the rollout targeted. A row with no running
    revision has nothing running yet and is skipped."""
    if ir_items is None:
        return
    for it in ir_items:
        comp = (it.get("spec") or {}).get("component", "?")
        st = it.get("status") or {}
        target = _rollout_done_target(comp, st, isvc_status)
        if target is None:
            continue
        try:
            rows = irstatus.instance_statuses(st)
        except irstatus.DecodeError:
            continue   # invariant A reports an undecodable status
        want = _rev_hash(target)
        inv["h_seen"] = True
        for row in rows or []:
            running = row.get("runningRevision") or ""
            if not running or _rev_hash(running) == want:
                continue
            idx = str(row.get("index", "?"))
            key = ("H", "superseded-instance", comp, idx)
            _inv_hit(inv, hits, key, key, INV_SUSTAIN_SETTLE, now,
                     f"{comp}/{idx} runs revision {_rev_hash(running)} after the rollout reported done on "
                     f"{want} (IR runningRevision={running}, updateRevision={target})")
        for pname, p in sorted(pod_state.items()):
            if p and p["alive"] and p["comp"] == comp and p.get("hash") and p["hash"] != want:
                key = ("H", "superseded-pod", comp, pname)
                _inv_hit(inv, hits, key, key, INV_SUSTAIN_SETTLE, now,
                         f"{comp}/{p.get('inst', '0')} pod {pname} carries {REV_LABEL}={p['hash']} "
                         f"after the rollout reported done on {want}")


def _list_podgroups(case_id):
    """name → spec.minMember for the case's PodGroups; None when the API is unavailable."""
    r = kubectl("-n", NS, "get", "podgroups.scheduling.x-k8s.io", "-l",
                f"ome.io/inferenceservice={case_id}", "-o", "json")
    if r.returncode != 0:
        return None
    try:
        items = json.loads(r.stdout).get("items", [])
    except Exception:
        return None
    return {(it.get("metadata") or {}).get("name", ""): int((it.get("spec") or {}).get("minMember") or 0)
            for it in items}


def _inv_fetch_ledger(case_id):
    """The rows of the service's audit ledger ConfigMap: [] while the
    ConfigMap does not exist, None when it cannot be read this tick."""
    r = kubectl("-n", NS, "get", "cm", f"{case_id}{AUDIT_LEDGER_SUFFIX}", "-o", "json")
    if r.returncode != 0:
        return [] if "not found" in (r.stderr or "").lower() else None
    try:
        hist = json.loads(json.loads(r.stdout).get("data", {}).get(AUDIT_LEDGER_KEY, "{}"))
        return hist.get("entries", []) or []
    except (ValueError, TypeError, AttributeError):
        return None


def _inv_check_auto_recover(inv, ledger, hits, now):
    """Invariant J, one tick: the service's audit ledger holds no AutoRecover
    record. The engine writes one when it gives up on an Instance's node and
    steers the rebuild elsewhere; a case that selects J says nothing it does
    should provoke that. A None ledger makes no observation. One tick is
    enough: a ledger row is durable, not a transition."""
    if ledger is None:
        return
    inv["j_seen"] = True
    for entry in ledger:
        if str(entry.get("reason") or "") != AUTO_RECOVER_REASON:
            continue
        comp, idx = str(entry.get("component") or "?"), str(entry.get("sourceInstance", "?"))
        key = ("J", "auto-recover", comp, idx)
        _inv_hit(inv, hits, key, key, 1, now,
                 f"{comp}/{idx}: the audit ledger records an {AUTO_RECOVER_REASON} entry "
                 f"(fromNode={entry.get('fromNode') or '?'} revision={str(entry.get('revision') or '?')[-12:]} "
                 f"phase={entry.get('phase') or '?'} outcome={entry.get('outcome') or '?'})")


def _inv_check_node_exclusion(inv, pod_state, hits, now):
    """Invariant K, one tick: no live pod of the service carries a required
    kubernetes.io/hostname NotIn term. The engine writes one only to keep an
    Instance's rebuild off a node it gave up on; a case that selects K says
    no placement of its pods may be narrowed that way. A record without the
    field (another watcher builder) is not evaluated."""
    for name, p in sorted(pod_state.items()):
        if not (p and p["alive"]) or "excl" not in p:
            continue
        inv["k_seen"] = True
        if not p["excl"]:
            continue
        key = ("K", "node-exclusion", p.get("comp", "?"), name)
        _inv_hit(inv, hits, key, key, 1, now,
                 f"{p.get('comp', '?')}/{p.get('inst', '?')} pod {name} carries a required "
                 f"{HOSTNAME_LABEL} NotIn [{', '.join(p['excl'])}] node affinity term")


def _inv_check_gang_scheduling(inv, pod_state, pods_per_inst, hits, now):
    """Invariant D, one tick, only when OME_EVAL_SCHEDULER names a scheduler:
    D1 every live case pod carries that schedulerName (the runtime's name
       reached the rendered pods); D2 every multi-pod Instance's pods share
       one pod-group label whose PodGroup exists with minMember == pods per
       Instance; D3 a gang binds as a unit — once any member has a node, every
       existing member has one within INV_SUSTAIN_D ticks. Teardown is not a
       gang event: pods being deleted are not counted."""
    live = [p for p in pod_state.values() if p and p["alive"]]
    untyped = [p for p in live if "sched" not in p or "pg" not in p or "node" not in p]
    if untyped:
        inv["d_untyped"] = True   # a record builder drifted: reported, never a violation
        live = [p for p in live if p not in untyped]
    if not live:
        return
    inv["d_seen"] = True
    for p in live:
        if p.get("sched", "") != SCHED_NAME:
            key = ("D", "scheduler-name", p["comp"], p.get("inst", "0"))
            _inv_hit(inv, hits, key, key, 1, now,
                     f"{p['comp']}/{p.get('inst', '0')} pod runs under scheduler "
                     f"{p.get('sched') or 'default'!r}, expected {SCHED_NAME!r}")
    gangs = defaultdict(list)
    for p in live:
        if pods_per_inst.get(p["comp"], 1) > 1:
            gangs[(p["comp"], p.get("inst", "0"))].append(p)
    if not gangs:
        return
    pgs = None
    for (comp, inst), members in sorted(gangs.items()):
        want = pods_per_inst[comp]
        bound = [m for m in members if m.get("node")]
        if bound and len(bound) < len(members):
            key = ("D", "partial-gang", comp, inst)
            _inv_hit(inv, hits, key, key, INV_SUSTAIN_D, now,
                     f"{comp}/{inst}: {len(bound)} of {len(members)} live gang pods bound to a node "
                     f"(gang size {want}) — the gang did not bind as a unit")
        groups = {m.get("pg", "") for m in members}
        if len(groups) != 1 or "" in groups:
            key = ("D", "pod-group-label", comp, inst)
            _inv_hit(inv, hits, key, key, INV_SUSTAIN_D, now,
                     f"{comp}/{inst}: gang pods carry pod-group labels {sorted(groups)!r}, expected one shared group")
            continue
        if pgs is None:
            pgs = _list_podgroups(inv["case_id"])
            if pgs is None:
                inv["pg_unavailable"] = True
                continue
        name = next(iter(groups))
        inv["pg_seen"] = True
        if name not in pgs:
            key = ("D", "pod-group-missing", comp, inst)
            _inv_hit(inv, hits, key, key, INV_SUSTAIN_D, now,
                     f"{comp}/{inst}: pods reference PodGroup {name!r}, which does not exist")
        elif pgs[name] != want:
            key = ("D", "pod-group-minmember", comp, inst)
            _inv_hit(inv, hits, key, key, 1, now,
                     f"{comp}/{inst}: PodGroup {name!r} minMember={pgs[name]}, expected {want}")


def _inv_any_on(inv):
    return any(inv.get(k) for k in ("a_on", "b_on", "c_on", "d_on", "f_on", "g_on", "h_on", "j_on", "k_on", "ratio"))


def _inv_tick(inv, pod_state, pods_per_inst):
    """One invariant observation, self-rate-limited to INV_TICK_S. Called from
    every watch loop each iteration; a no-op between ticks and when every
    invariant is opted out. Reads the cluster once per tick and hands the
    snapshots to _inv_observe."""
    if not inv or not _inv_any_on(inv):
        return
    now = time.time()
    if now - inv["last"] < INV_TICK_S:
        return
    inv["last"] = now
    case_id = inv["case_id"]
    ir_items = _inv_fetch_ir_items(case_id) if (inv["a_on"] or inv["g_on"] or inv["h_on"]) else None
    routing = _inv_fetch_routing(case_id) if (inv["b_on"] or inv["g_on"]) else None
    isvc_status = fetch_status(case_id) if inv["h_on"] else None
    revisions = (_inv_fetch_revisions(case_id)
                 if inv["f_on"] and _inv_revisions_wanted(inv, pod_state) else None)
    ledger = _inv_fetch_ledger(case_id) if inv.get("j_on") else None
    _inv_observe(inv, pod_state, pods_per_inst, now, ir_items=ir_items, routing=routing,
                 isvc_status=isvc_status, revisions=revisions, ledger=ledger)


def _inv_observe(inv, pod_state, pods_per_inst, now, ir_items=None, routing=None,
                 isvc_status=None, revisions=None, ledger=None):
    """One observation over already-fetched snapshots: every enabled check
    runs, then streaks reset for keys not observed this tick (the
    CONSECUTIVE-tick sustain rule). Pure, so tests drive ticks with synthetic
    pods, InferenceReplicas, Services and revisions. A None snapshot is one
    that could not be read this tick: its checks make no observation."""
    hits = set()
    if inv["a_on"]:
        _inv_check_status_truth(inv, pod_state, pods_per_inst, ir_items, hits, now)
    if inv["b_on"]:
        _inv_check_endpoints(inv, pod_state, routing, hits, now)
    if inv["c_on"]:
        _inv_check_pair_alive(inv, pod_state, hits, now)
    if inv.get("d_on"):
        _inv_check_gang_scheduling(inv, pod_state, pods_per_inst, hits, now)
    if inv.get("ratio"):
        _inv_check_cohort_ratio(inv, pod_state, pods_per_inst, now)
    if inv["f_on"]:
        if revisions is not None:
            _inv_learn_revisions(inv, pod_state, revisions)
        _inv_check_label_truth(inv, pod_state, hits, now)
    if inv["g_on"]:
        _inv_check_ready_serving(inv, pod_state, pods_per_inst, ir_items, routing, hits, now)
    if inv["h_on"]:
        _inv_check_superseded(inv, pod_state, ir_items, isvc_status, hits, now)
    if inv.get("j_on"):
        _inv_check_auto_recover(inv, ledger, hits, now)
    if inv.get("k_on"):
        _inv_check_node_exclusion(inv, pod_state, hits, now)
    for k in [k for k in inv["streaks"] if k not in hits]:
        del inv["streaks"][k]


def invariant_checks(inv, verdict, notes, checks):
    """Verdict gate for the continuous invariants: every violation that fired
    (sustained past its carve-out) FAILs the case, with first/last-seen
    timestamps and the tick occurrence count. The one exception is a parked
    case whose header scopes its tracked bug to an invariant class
    (inv_xfail): violations of exactly that class record as the case's
    known-bug XFAIL — still evaluated, still printed — while any other class
    fails hard, so unrelated regressions can never hide behind the parking."""
    if not inv:
        return verdict
    if inv["off"]:
        checks.append(f"  ⓘ continuous invariant(s) disabled by header inv_off={inv['off']} (reason in the case file)")
    if inv["a_on"] and not inv["ir_seen"]:
        checks.append("  ⓘ invariant A (status-truth) skipped — IR instanceStatuses unavailable on this build")
    if inv["b_on"] and not inv["b_seen"]:
        checks.append("  ⓘ invariant B (endpoints-membership) evaluated zero Ready+serving pods against a routed Service — vacuous (no assertion made)")
    pairing = inv.get("pairing")
    if inv["c_on"] and pairing and not pairing.get("seen"):
        checks.append("  ⓘ invariant C (pair-alive) never saw both engine and decoder serving at a tick — vacuous (no assertion made)")
    if inv.get("d_on") and not inv.get("d_seen"):
        checks.append("  ⓘ invariant D (gang-scheduling) never saw a live pod — vacuous (no assertion made)")
    if inv.get("d_on") and inv.get("pg_unavailable"):
        checks.append("  ⓘ invariant D: PodGroup API unavailable on this cluster — pod-group checks skipped; scheduler name and gang binding still asserted")
    if inv.get("d_on") and inv.get("d_untyped"):
        checks.append("  ⓘ invariant D: some pod records carried no placement fields (a watcher builder lacks _pod_placement) — those records were not evaluated")
    if inv.get("f_on") and not inv.get("f_seen"):
        checks.append("  ⓘ invariant F (label-truth) compared no pod against its revision's template — vacuous (no assertion made)")
    if inv.get("f_on") and inv.get("mutated_uids"):
        touched = ", ".join(f"{name} ({uid[:8]})" for uid, name in sorted(inv["mutated_uids"].items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1]))
        checks.append(f"  ⓘ invariant F: {len(inv['mutated_uids'])} pod(s) whose spec the harness changed itself were not judged: {touched}")
    if inv.get("g_on") and not inv.get("g_seen"):
        checks.append("  ⓘ invariant G (ready-serving) never saw a Ready Instance with its pod set Ready — vacuous (no assertion made)")
    if inv.get("g_on") and inv.get("g_seen") and not inv.get("g_routing_seen"):
        checks.append("  ⓘ invariant G: no routed Service observed — the serving gate was asserted, endpoint membership was not")
    if inv.get("h_on") and not inv.get("h_seen"):
        checks.append("  ⓘ invariant H (superseded-revision) never saw a Component report its rollout done — vacuous (no assertion made)")
    if inv.get("j_on") and not inv.get("j_seen"):
        checks.append("  ⓘ invariant J (no-auto-recovery) never read the audit ledger — vacuous (no assertion made)")
    if inv.get("k_on") and not inv.get("k_seen"):
        checks.append("  ⓘ invariant K (no-node-exclusion) never saw a live pod's node affinity — vacuous (no assertion made)")
    ratio = inv.get("ratio")
    if ratio:
        tol_pct = int(round(ratio["tol"] * 100))
        if not ratio["samples"]:
            checks.append("  ⓘ invariant E (cohort ratio) never saw canary capacity on both engine and decoder at a tick — vacuous (informational)")
        elif not ratio["excursions"]:
            checks.append(f"  ⓘ invariant E (cohort ratio, informational): the canary cohort stayed within {tol_pct}% of the fleet ratio across {ratio['samples']} tick(s)")
        else:
            checks.append(f"  ⚠ invariant E (cohort ratio, informational): {ratio['excursions']} sustained excursion(s) beyond {tol_pct}%, worst {int(round(ratio['worst'] * 100))}% — {ratio['worst_detail']}")
    if not inv["viol"]:
        active = [x for x, on in (("A", inv["a_on"] and inv["ir_seen"]),
                                  ("B", inv["b_on"] and inv["b_seen"]),
                                  ("C", inv["c_on"] and bool(pairing) and pairing.get("seen", False)),
                                  ("D", inv.get("d_on", False) and inv.get("d_seen", False)),
                                  ("F", inv.get("f_on", False) and inv.get("f_seen", False)),
                                  ("G", inv.get("g_on", False) and inv.get("g_seen", False)),
                                  ("H", inv.get("h_on", False) and inv.get("h_seen", False)),
                                  ("J", inv.get("j_on", False) and inv.get("j_seen", False)),
                                  ("K", inv.get("k_on", False) and inv.get("k_seen", False))) if on]
        if active:
            checks.append(f"  ✓ continuous invariants held ({'+'.join(active)}): no sustained "
                          f"{' / '.join(INV_NAMES[x] for x in active)} violation")
        return verdict
    scope = inv.get("xfail") or ""
    ref = f"#{inv['xfail_issue']}" if inv.get("xfail_issue") else "UNLINKED"
    expected_hits = 0
    for key, v in sorted(inv["viol"].items()):
        first = time.strftime("%H:%M:%S", time.localtime(v["first"]))
        last = time.strftime("%H:%M:%S", time.localtime(v["last"]))
        span = f"[first {first}, last {last}, {v['n']} tick(s)]"
        if scope == "all" or key[0] == scope:
            expected_hits += 1
            notes.append(f"invariant {key[0]} {key[1]} (known bug: {ref}): {v['detail']}")
            checks.append(f"  ⓘ invariant {key[0]} violated ({key[1]}) — the tracked bug "
                          f"this case is parked on ({ref}): {v['detail']} {span}")
        else:
            verdict = "FAIL"
            notes.append(f"invariant {key[0]} {key[1]}: {v['detail']}")
            checks.append(f"  ✗ invariant {key[0]} violated ({key[1]}): {v['detail']} {span}")
    if expected_hits and verdict == "PASS":
        verdict = f"XFAIL (known bug: {ref})"
    return verdict


# ── Fault injection (header fault=<kind>:<param>) ───────────────────────────
# Runner plumbing for controlled faults. Kinds:
#   quota:<n>          — pre-trigger: create a namespace ResourceQuota sized from
#                        the case's OWN pod requests (never hardcoded) to admit
#                        exactly current-usage + n more pods of the case's shape.
#   podkill:<phase>    — at the phase hook, delete one deterministic pod.
#   ctrlrestart:<phase>— at the phase hook, delete the OME manager pod. ALWAYS
#                        gated on OME_TEST_ALLOW_CTRL_RESTART=1 (shared-cluster
#                        safety); otherwise skipped with an ⓘ note. In canary
#                        mode ctrlrestart:idle fires before the bump and waits
#                        for the manager, and its webhook, to come back, so
#                        the arm is the restarted manager's.
#   webhook:<phase>    — at idle (with during=idle) or as the operation lands
#                        (settling): point the admission webhook's Service at
#                        no pod until lift=after-hold|after-window, then put
#                        it back; every write the webhooks intercept is
#                        refused meanwhile, status writes pass.
#   conflict:<phase>   — at the same phases: a competing writer patches an
#                        annotation of target=isvc|ir once (form=once) or at
#                        CONFLICT_RATE_HZ until the operation completes
#                        (form=persist), so the controller's status writes
#                        carry a stale resourceVersion.
#   cordon:source      — pre-trigger: cordon the node hosting the source pod;
#                        ALWAYS uncordoned in cleanup (failure-path safe).
#   crashloop:old      — at the settling hook, right after the bump: make one
#                        OLD-revision pod of the bumped engine crash on every
#                        start, for as long as it runs the old revision. The
#                        pod is the highest-index Instance's leader (or single)
#                        pod, so the roll reaches it last and the crash is
#                        observed on a settled row for the whole roll. form=
#                        picks the failure: start points the live pod at an
#                        image with no shell, so the fixture command dies at
#                        every start and the kubelet parks it in
#                        CrashLoopBackOff, never Ready again; load kills the
#                        runner (PID 1) every CRASH_KILL_INTERVAL_S while the
#                        container is up, so it dies after Ready and comes
#                        back between crashes. Only the image and an exec are
#                        available against a live pod, which is why neither
#                        form edits the template. The verdict adds: that
#                        Instance ends on the new revision and serving, and
#                        no RestartTriggered event names it after the bump.
#                        A gang under SurgeThenDrain is replaced at a fresh
#                        Instance index and its source index retired, so
#                        the verdict follows the Instance through its gang
#                        surges and reads the index it ended at: the pairs
#                        the status rows claimed while each surge was in
#                        flight, then the ones the ISVC events kept (a start
#                        names the replacement index; an abandon retires
#                        one), since the recorder drops events past a burst.
# Phase enum: settling (immediately after the trigger), rotating (first surge/
# updated pod observed post-trigger), migrating (migration accept observed).
# One firing per case (latched). Any fault-APPARATUS error → the distinct
# INFRA-FAIL verdict: the harness broke, not the product — never a FAIL/PASS.
# Canary-state hooks: the grid state the canary verb reads off the ISVC
# status each poll (Pending -> staging, Canarying/Paused -> serving,
# Promoting -> draining, RollingBack, Failed). A fault or a verb keyed on one
# fires while the step machine is in that state; "@<step>" narrows it to one
# step index.
CANARY_HOOKS = {"canary-staging", "canary-serving", "canary-prehold", "canary-draining", "canary-done",
                "canary-rollingback", "canary-rolledback", "canary-failed"}
